# Line-ending policy, modelled on ../MacQuadra800_MiSTer/.gitattributes.
#
# Text files we author are pinned to LF so a Windows build box (Quartus rewrites
# .qsf/.qpf with CRLF on every compile) or core.autocrlf never produces
# whole-file diffs.
*.sv          text eol=lf
*.qsf         text eol=lf
*.qpf         text eol=lf
*.sdc         text eol=lf
*.md          text eol=lf

# Executed/parsed by POSIX tools: CRLF is a hard failure, not cosmetic
# (a CRLF `#!/bin/sh` dies under WSL/macOS/MiSTer).
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.py          text eol=lf
*.tcl         text eol=lf
Makefile      text eol=lf
*.mk          text eol=lf

# Windows batch files: keep byte-exact as committed.
*.bat         -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binaries: never convert, never diff as text. ROMs and disk images contain
# stray CR bytes; one CRLF conversion silently corrupts them.
*.hda         binary
*.hdf         binary
*.hpi         binary
*.img         binary
*.iso         binary
*.chd         binary
*.rom         binary
*.bin         binary
*.BIN         binary
*.nvr         binary
*.tgz         binary
*.gz          binary
*.zip         binary
*.pdf         binary
*.png         binary
*.jpg         binary
*.rbf         binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT normalized, deliberately (checked out byte-exact as committed):
#
#   sys/**          vendored from ../Template_MiSTer. Renormalizing would turn
#                   every template sync into whole-file diffs.
#   rtl/ap68040/**  vendored from ../MacQuadra800_MiSTer (AP68040 by Adam
#                   Polkosnik). Keep byte-identical to upstream so re-syncs
#                   diff cleanly. See rtl/ap68040/UPSTREAM.md and docs/.
#   template demo rtl (mycore.v, lfsr.v, cos.sv) until Phase 0 replaces it.
sys/**              -text
rtl/ap68040/**      -text
rtl/mycore.v        -text
rtl/lfsr.v          -text
rtl/cos.sv          -text
HP9K385.srf         -text
